  "title": "Existing tools got better routes into Pollinations",
  "summary": "Pollinations grew into more of a working environment this week: existing clients got easier to connect, larger media fit through chat, and community work became easier to find and reward.\n\nPrompt agents can now return caller-defined function calls for clients to execute and replay, alongside server-run MCP tools. An Anthropic-compatible `/v1/messages` endpoint gives Claude Code and Anthropic SDKs another route to supported text models. Polli added setup for Codex, Claude Code, Hermes Agent and Pi, while new MCP account tools can handle usage, earnings, Quest status and API keys when permitted.\n\nThe text APIs first gained 32 MiB JSON requests; chat completions then expanded to 100 MiB for supported inline media. The gateway replaces large image, video and file data URIs with media URLs before sending them to providers, and later added handling for inline PDFs on OpenRouter models and base64 audio on Inkling. Individual offloaded items remain capped at 20 MiB, and provider URL support still varies. Uploads also grew to 400 MiB with streaming support in Polli.\n\nLightning Image Turbo added reference-guided images; HeyGen added short video with synchronized audio; and new transcription, stem-separation, speech, voice-changing and isolation options broadened the audio toolkit. Claude Sonnet 5.5, GPT-6.1 Sol and two decision models joined the catalog. The SDK and Polli gained more of these media operations, while video resolution declarations and fallback fixes made existing routes more predictable. Amazon Nova Canvas and Reel were retired on September 30; requests using their IDs return 400.\n\nThe API and Polli gained E2B Linux sandboxes that can be created, inspected and reached over SSH, with time paid from a Pollinations wallet in advance. Polli 0.1.23 includes create, list, kill and SSH-config commands. It is a new place to run code, not just another model to ask about running code.",
  "pr_count": 152,
